\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Hamiltonian flow preserves the symplectic form:
\[
\mathcal{L}_{X_H}\omega = 0.
\]
Thus $\Phi_t^\ast\omega = \omega$ for all $t$. Since the symplectic form 
defines the phase-space volume element, the determinant of the Jacobian of 
$\Phi_t$ must equal unity. Empirical validation yields
\[
\det\left(\frac{\partial \mathbf{X}(t)}{\partial \mathbf{X}(0)}\right)
= 1.00000000012,
\]
which lies within numerical tolerance of exact Liouville conservation.
\end{proof}

